# The English source strings for the key sheet, the OSD's modifier prefix and
# the sheet's own title -- everything bin/imthemousenow-lib.sh's t() and
# bin/imthemousenow-help look up by key.
#
# Loaded for English the same way any other locale's file would be, rather
# than special-cased out of the lookup -- every t() call also carries this
# same text as its own fallback ($2), so a missing file, a missing key, or a
# $PLUGIN_DIR too old to have a locale/ directory at all still reads correctly
# in English regardless. This file exists to be copied -- `cp en.strings
# de.strings`, then translate the right-hand side of each line and leave the
# keys alone. A locale file that only translates some of these keys is not a
# broken locale: whatever it leaves out falls back to the English here.
#
# `<code>.strings` is chosen from LC_MESSAGES or LANG (LANG=de_DE.UTF-8 reads
# as de) -- see _locale_name() in bin/imthemousenow-lib.sh.
#
# Not covered here: the seven ACTION display words (config.default.toml's
# `[imthemousenow.action.*]` `label` values), because that string currently
# doubles as the action's own config key -- translating it needs a schema
# change (splitting identifier from display label) before a strings file can
# hand it to a translator. The `--help` heredocs and docs/manual/ are separate,
# lower-priority tracks of their own.

